From: Samaksh Kamboj <samakshk4@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] NTCamera: guard empty Exif value in writeTagValue

ExifOutputStream.writeTagValue() zero-terminates ASCII/UNDEFINED values
in place:

    byte[] buf = tag.getStringByte();
    if (buf.length == tag.getComponentCount()) {
        buf[buf.length - 1] = 0;   // <- line 721
        out.write(buf);
    } else {
        out.write(buf);
        out.write(0);
    }

When a tag carries an empty byte array (buf.length == componentCount ==
0) the buffer is written at index -1, throwing
ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException and crashing JPEG write-out. Skip the
terminator write when the array is empty.

---
diff --git a/smali_classes4/com/ape/utils/exif/ExifOutputStream.smali b/smali_classes4/com/ape/utils/exif/ExifOutputStream.smali
index 0534bc5..1421225 100644
--- a/smali_classes4/com/ape/utils/exif/ExifOutputStream.smali
+++ b/smali_classes4/com/ape/utils/exif/ExifOutputStream.smali
@@ -2569,10 +2569,13 @@
     .line 721
     array-length p0, v0
 
+    if-eqz p0, :cond_empty
+
     add-int/lit8 p0, p0, -0x1
 
     aput-byte v1, v0, p0
 
+    :cond_empty
     .line 722
     invoke-virtual {p1, v0}, Lcom/ape/utils/exif/OrderedDataOutputStream;->write([B)V
 
